Description: MIDI controllers as a KDE Plasma control deck
 Chimp turns MIDI controllers into a control deck for the KDE Plasma
 desktop: knobs for system, focused-app, playing-app and game volume,
 brightness and microphone; pads for mute, media keys, shortcuts, apps,
 commands and OBS scenes. It shows live values on the device's pad
 lights and in an on-screen overlay.
 .
 It also replaces Akai's editor for the LPD8 mk2 (pads, knobs, programs
 over SysEx), and learns any class-compliant controller (Teenage
 Engineering KO II, Arturia MicroFreak and others) into profiles.
 .
 Chimp Loop plays a drum kit from any controller and loops it, quantised
 or not, with overdub layers, and exports loops as WAV or MIDI files.
